# .easignore — what EAS Build uploads.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE EDITING. When this file exists, eas-cli uses it INSTEAD of
# .gitignore. Every rule .gitignore was carrying — node_modules/, venv/, .env,
# the *.sql dumps — stops applying to the upload. So this file is written as an
# ALLOWLIST: ignore everything, then name only what a mobile build needs. A
# denylist would have to restate the whole of .gitignore, and one omission
# uploads a secret.
#
# Concretely: packages/mobile/.env is gitignored and holds the *secret* Mapbox
# download token (sk.*). It sits inside the one directory this file re-includes,
# so the exclusion in section 5 is load-bearing, not defensive.
#
# Paths are relative to the WORKSPACE ROOT — npm workspaces makes that the
# archive root, not packages/mobile.
#
# Measured 2026-09-08: 314 MB / 1856 tracked files in, ~6 MB out.
# packages/auxein-marketing alone is 198 MB, docs/ 77 MB, bfg.jar 14 MB.
#
# This file is hashed into the fingerprint (eas-cli hashes eas.json AND
# .easignore), so editing it bumps the runtimeVersion on BOTH platforms and
# orphans every binary already built. Change it in the same commit as a build.

# ---- 1. Everything at the root ------------------------------------------
/*

# ---- 2. The workspace manifests the install needs -----------------------
# npm reads every workspace's package.json to resolve the tree, so a missing
# one breaks `npm ci` even though the mobile bundle never touches that package.
# None of the six packages has a prepare/postinstall script, so the manifest
# alone is enough — no sources required.
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
!/packages
/packages/*/*
!/packages/*/package.json

# ---- 3. The only package actually built ---------------------------------
# packages/shared is deliberately NOT here: metro.config.js blockLists it,
# along with web, insights and marketing, so its source can never enter the
# bundle. Its package.json is already kept by section 2.
!/packages/mobile/**

# ---- 4. Re-exclude the build junk section 3 just pulled back in ----------
/packages/mobile/node_modules/
/packages/mobile/.expo/
/packages/mobile/dist/
/packages/mobile/web-build/
/packages/mobile/.metro-health-check*
/packages/mobile/*.tsbuildinfo

# ---- 5. Secrets and signing material ------------------------------------
/packages/mobile/.env
/packages/mobile/.env.*
/packages/mobile/*.jks
/packages/mobile/*.p8
/packages/mobile/*.p12
/packages/mobile/*.key
/packages/mobile/*.mobileprovision
/packages/mobile/*.pem

# ---- 6. CNG: the native dirs must never be uploaded ----------------------
# @expo/fingerprint decides managed vs bare by asking whether
# android/app/build.gradle exists AND is un-ignored. An uploaded native dir
# flips the builder to bare after it prebuilds; it then hashes android/ instead
# of the config plugins, the runtimeVersion stops matching the one eas-cli
# computed locally, and the build dies in "Configure expo-updates". That was
# the six consecutive failures of build 10. Neither dir exists on this machine
# today — these lines are here so a stray `expo prebuild` cannot resurrect the
# bug.
/packages/mobile/android/
/packages/mobile/ios/
